{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>If the spirit.</b> Because he mentioned above that the words of the wise are heeded more than the words of a ruler over fools, he comes back to caution the wise man: if you have risen through your wisdom to the rank of government, as in the matter of \"from the house of prisoners he goes out to rule\" — do not leave your place. The meaning is: lowness of spirit. Or its meaning is that he should continue to engage in wisdom constantly, as he did at first, as though he never moved from his place and never rose to a higher rank among men. And know that if you slacken, the slackening will leave you with great sins. And it is more accurate that <b>marpe</b> is a verb of the heavy stem [binyan kaved], from which comes <i>herpeah</i>, the alef in place of the heh, like <b>alef</b> therefore it is <b>marpe</b>, which is from the heavy stem, and the meaning is that one who abandons government will leave behind great sins. And some say: \"a healing man leaves great sins,\" like a master of medicine who does not eat anything that will greatly harm him, but rather guards himself. And this commentator interprets: if the spirit of the ruler — that is, the anger of the ruler — rises upon you, do not depart from the discourse of wisdom, and the wise man will not anger the ruler. And the meaning is that the wise man will leave behind every matter that brings him to a sin on account of which the ruler would be angered, like the physician who guards against harmful foods at the outset."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The verse phrase כי מבית הסורים יצא למלוך is quoted from Ecclesiastes 4:14. The phrase 'כאל״ף על כן' is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally as 'like alef therefore.' The Hebrew switches between second and third person without signal; preserved as-is."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:55.786491830Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}